```
1. Delegate focus-routing keydown handling to child components; commit event contract
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/clanker-app.js': Remove key-routing; retain only zone-agnostic keys + Ctrl+I
        - Removed `#selectedElement`, `#inputActions`, `#messageActions`, and the combo-lookup routing in `#handleGlobalKeydown`
        - `#handleGlobalKeydown` handles only: Ctrl+I (toggle keyboard-bar), Ctrl+Enter (copySelected), Alt+Enter (ingestSelected), Ctrl+1 (toggleReasoning), Ctrl+2 (toggleContent)
        - Added listeners for child-dispatched events:
            - `toggle-scroll-lock` → `messagesBox.toggleScrollLock()`
            - `focus-message` → switch(detail): `'first'` → selectFirst, `'last'` → selectLast
            - `focus-input` → `inputBox.focus()`
        - Renamed `prompt-fired` listener to `prompt-selected`
        - In `#generateResponse` finally block: removed `#selectedElement` read; kept only `this.inputBox.setDisabled(false)`
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/input-box.js': Add keydown handling for zone-specific keys
        - Ctrl+ArrowUp → dispatch `focus-message` detail `'last'`, stopPropagation + preventDefault
        - Ctrl+ArrowDown → dispatch `focus-message` detail `'first'`, stopPropagation + preventDefault
        - Escape → dispatch `toggle-scroll-lock`, stopPropagation + preventDefault
        - Kept existing Enter (no-modifier) → `#dispatchSubmit()` as-is
        - No knowledge of messages-box; only dispatches upward
        - Replaced `disabled` textarea approach with `#halted` bool: textarea stays enabled (focus retained), `#dispatchSubmit` returns early when halted, send button greyed via its own `disabled` attribute
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/messages-box.js': Extend keydown handler to own zone-specific navigation + Escape
        - Ctrl+ArrowUp → `selectPreviousMsg()`, stopPropagation + preventDefault
        - Ctrl+ArrowDown → `selectNextMsg()`, stopPropagation + preventDefault
        - If navigation fails (at boundary) → dispatch `focus-input`, stopPropagation + preventDefault
        - Escape → dispatch `focus-input`, stopPropagation + preventDefault
        - Restructured guard order: handle Ctrl+Arrow combos first, then Escape, then block remaining ctrl/alt (let zone-agnostic keys bubble to document), then handle plain arrow/page scrolling
        - Plain ArrowUp/ArrowDown/PageUp/PageDown scrolling: unchanged
        - `#selectedMsg` tracking stays unchanged
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/keyboard-bar.js': Rename event
        - Dispatch `prompt-selected` instead of `prompt-fired`
        - No other structural change; stopPropagation retained
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/api-client.js': No change
        - Streaming callbacks (onToken, onReasoning, onPrefill) remain callbacks
